<title>UK: LIFFE details May certified stock data.</title>
<headline>LIFFE details May certified stock data.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>LIFFE certified coffee stocks totalled 881 five-tonne lots in May compared with 4,858 in April, the exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>The sharp fall in stocks recorded was because of a change in the grading system.</p>
<p>LIFFE said the data relate to coffee certified as tenderable under the new grading terms which take effect from the July delivery contract onwards.</p>
<p>The 4,858 lots graded in April cease to be valid if not tendered by the end of of May.</p>
<p>For May coffee, members have an option of grading under the new or the old system which expired at the end of May. Coffee graded under the old rules will have to be re-graded.</p>
<p>Following is the breakdown in May certified stocks, in fove-tonne lots.</p>
<p>			    MAY	  APRIL</p>
<p>United Kingdom	    0	    2</p>
<p>Rotterdam		 135	  301</p>
<p>Amsterdam		 nil	  nil</p>
<p>Hamburg		   nil	  188</p>
<p>Bremen			6	  134</p>
<p>Antwerp		   294	2,245</p>
<p>Le Harve		  145	  341</p>
<p>Barcelona		  23	  364</p>
<p>Trieste		     4	   15</p>
<p>New York		   23	    2</p>
<p>New Orleans	     251	1,266</p>
<p>Total		     881	4,858</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
